###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/DataProcessingAndAnalysis
:DataProcessingAndAnalysis rdf:type owl:Class ;
                           rdfs:subClassOf :HazardModes ;
                           rdfs:comment "Data processing and analysis are necessary stages in healthcare, where raw data is transformed into actionable insights to inform clinical decisions. However, these stages are prone to various hazards, including technical flaws, biases, and errors in interpretation. Understanding and mitigating these hazards is essential for ensuring the accuracy, reliability, and fairness of data-driven healthcare decisions. The risks associated with data processing and analysis, such as inaccuracies, algorithmic bias, overfitting, and real-time processing failures, can have significant consequences for patient outcomes if not properly managed." .


