               rdfs:comment "These methods combine various methods for generating healthcare synthetic data, including statistical, simulation-based, rule-based, and machine learning-based. By leveraging the strengths of multiple methods, hybrid methods may result in improved diversity, utility, and realism. These methods have vast applications, such as predictive modeling, health resource allocation, and clinical decision support systems." .


