###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/RuledBasedMethods
:RuledBasedMethods rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf :SyntheticDataGenerationMethods ;
                   rdfs:comment "Rule-based (a.k.a. knowledge-driven) methods rely on expert opinion and predefined rules for generating synthetic data. Some rule-based methods rely on external sources of medical information, such as knowledge bases and guidelines like Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMEDCT), which include patient medical conditions, protocols used for treatment, and diagnosis. Other rulebased synthetic data generation methods are based on scripted generation and are hence more internal, as they involve scripts for simulating clinical workflows, patient history, patient trajectories, and disease progress. Such methods help ensure that the synthetic data is closely aligned with real-world clinical data, as they can impose constraints that follow from domain knowledge, for example, logical constraints regarding indications and contra-indications, which is not directly possible in statistical or machine learning methods." .


