###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/SimulationBasedMethods
:SimulationBasedMethods rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf :SyntheticDataGenerationMethods ;
                        rdfs:comment "These methods can conduct simulations regarding the spread of disease, physiological processes, and allocation of health resources for generating synthetic healthcare data. Monte Carlo simulations generate synthetic data for specific random variables by drawing from a probability distribution created by repeated sampling and have, for example, been used to synthesise tabular inpatient claim data. Agent-based models read the interactions and dynamics at the individual level to provide an overview of the health dynamics of a more abstract level like society. Physics-based simulations can help generate synthetic data for designing and evaluating medical devices and physiological processes. These methods can help understand healthcare systems and devices and their complexities and optimize decision-making" .


