###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/StatisticalMethods
:StatisticalMethods rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf :SyntheticDataGenerationMethods ;
                    rdfs:comment "These methods consist of parametric and non-parametric statistical models for generating healthcare synthetic data. Parametric statistical models presuppose a particular functional form based on a finite, fixed set of parameters. For example, logistic regression can be used to generate synthetic healthcare data. In contrast, nonparametric statistical models do not presuppose a particular functional form nor a finite, fixed set of parameters, thereby providing flexibility and adaptability for generating synthetic healthcare data. Examples are resampling methods and Kernel Density Estimation (KDE). The KDE is a non-parametric method used to estimate the probability distribution of a population based on a finite sample." .


