###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#FalsePositives/NegativesInPredictiveModeling
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#FalsePositives/NegativesInPredictiveModeling> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                                         :DataProcessingAndAnalysis ;
                                                                                                                :HasConsequence <http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#UnnecessaryTreatments;MissedDiagnoses> ;
                                                                                                                :HasDetectability :MediumDetectability ;
                                                                                                                :HasLikelihood :MediumLikelihood ;
                                                                                                                :HasMitigation :BalanceDatasets ,
                                                                                                                               :RecalibrationTechniques ;
                                                                                                                :HasPotentialCause <http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#ModelOverfitting;ImbalancedDatasets> ;
                                                                                                                :HasSeverity :HighSeverity ;
                                                                                                                :HasDetectabilityScore 6 ;
                                                                                                                :HasLikelihoodScore 6 ;
                                                                                                                :HasSeverityScore 8 ;
                                                                                                                rdfs:comment """Predictive models may generate false positives (incorrect predictions of outcomes) or false negatives (failing to predict outcomes), leading to unnecessary treatments or missed diagnoses. Causes include model overfitting, imbalanced datasets, and inadequate validation. Consequences involve patient distress from false positives or harm from missed diagnoses. Mitigation strategies include using balanced datasets, thorough cross-validation, and recalibration techniques to reduce prediction errors.

In healthcare diagnostics, false positives can lead to unnecessary treatments, while false negatives can result in missed diagnoses, both of which are potentially life-threatening. The likelihood and detectability of these errors are often medium, as despite improvements in AI and data analysis, these errors remain due to variability in healthcare data quality and challenges in training accurate models. Moreover, these errors can often be detected through quality assurance methods, such as cross-validation in predictive models. Still, detection can be challenging when working with vast amounts of data. Moreover, Alex R., et al. mentioned that, in medicine, there is a well-established principle that the lower the prevalence of any given condition, the higher the likelihood for false positives for even the most accurate diagnostic test.""" .


