###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#ISO/IEC20889Standard
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#ISO/IEC20889Standard> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                                 :IEC ,
                                                                                                 :ISO ;
                                                                                        rdfs:comment """At the core of ISO/IEC 20889 lies a technical model that conceptualises re-identification risk through a structured taxonomy of attributes. The standard distinguishes between direct identifiers, indirect identifiers, quasi-identifiers, sensitive attributes, and local identifiers, clarifying that identifiability does not stem merely from the presence of overt identifiers, but from the interplay of attributes that, when combined, allow an individual to be singled out either within the dataset or against external sources. For health datasets, this taxonomy is essential because quasi-identifiers often emerge in subtle and  highly contextualised ways. Attributes such as the date of admission to a specialised clinic, the
presence of a rare diagnosis, or the conjunction of age, sex, and geographical indicators can, as demonstrated in Annex A of the standard, produce unique or  near-unique patterns that collapse the anonymity set""" .


