###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/AtnAEs
:AtnAEs rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 :AutoencoderBasedGenerationModels ;
        rdfs:comment "Attention-based Autoencoders (AtnAEs) integrate attention mechanisms into the autoencoding framework, enhancing representation learning by focusing on the most relevant features of the input data. This approach allows for improved capture and reconstruction of complex data patterns, making them highly effective for tasks requiring detailed focus, such as image captioning and natural language processing. Attention-based Autoencoders are carefully designed with detailed documentation of their integration of attention mechanisms, training procedures, and evaluation metrics to ensure transparency and reproducibility. The models typically employ learning rates ranging from 0.0004 to 0.001 to stabilize the training process and ensure convergence. Authors employed the Adam optimizer with a fixed learning rate of 0.001 and a batch size of 256 to model incomplete multi-modal data and dynamically capture the adjacency semantic correlation for cross-modal retrieval, and authors employed the same hyperparameters and vary the learning rates from 0.0004 to 0.0001 to predict Transcription Factor target (TF-target) gene interactions. In NLP, these models excel in tasks such as machine translation, text summarization, and sentiment analysis by focusing on relevant parts of the text, improving contextual understanding. Moreover, attention mechanisms alleviate tasks like speech recognition and music generation by focusing on relevant audio input segments, improving the generated output quality." .


