###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/AttnGAN
:AttnGAN rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :GANs ;
         :GeneratesModality :ImageData ,
                            :TextData ,
                            :TimeSeriesData ;
         :UsesTechnique :AdversarialAutoencoders ,
                        :AttentionSelfAttentionMechanism ,
                        :BatchNormalisation ,
                        :FeatureMatching ,
                        :LatentSpaceEncodingAdjustmentManipulationInterpolationRegularisation ,
                        :NoiseInjection ,
                        :SemanticHashing ;
         rdfs:comment "Attention GAN (AttnGAN) enhances traditional GANs by incorporating attention mechanisms within its architecture to generate realistic and detailed synthetic images, focusing on the most significant data features. This approach significantly improves generated images’ accuracy and contextual relevance, making AttnGAN particularly effective for applications requiring high-detail synthesis. AttnGAN is designed to strongly emphasize transparency and reproducibility, providing detailed documentation of its architecture, training processes, and evaluation metrics. It typically employs learning rates similar to those used in other GAN variants, ranging from 0.0001 to 0.0002, to stabilize the training process and ensure convergence. Different authors used different batch sizes with respect to their requirements for balancing computational efficiency with model performance, such as 1, 4, and 64, and utilized Adam optimizers to effectively minimize the loss functions. This model supports image and text data." .


