###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/AttributeInferenceRisk
:AttributeInferenceRisk rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                 :PrivacyAgainstInference ;
                        rdfs:comment "Attribute inference occurs when an attacker has (partial) information about a particular individual and uses that information to derive additional attributes, such as medication use or diagnosis. When published, synthetic data can potentially be used to train an inference model. An example is the k-nearest neighbor classifier used to estimate unknown properties of a randomly drawn ‘leaked/compromised’ sample of the real data from synthetic samples that are close to the real samples. If this can be done accurately, it indicates privacy risk when disclosing synthetic data. Attribute Inference Risk is often modeled in the context of generating EHR." .


