###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/AuthenticityScore
:AuthenticityScore rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                            :FidelityMetrics ,
                            :GeneralisationMetrics ,
                            :RecordSimilarity ;
                   :HasModality :TabularData ;
                   rdfs:comment "To investigate whether synthetic samples are truly novel samples or simply real training samples with some added noise, develop the sample-wise binary authenticity score. Here, the score is 1 if the closest point to a real datapoint is a synthetic datapoint and 0 if this is a real datapoint. When aggregated, it should be at least random whether the closest data point to a real data point is synthetic or real. So, the maximum average score would be 0.5; any score significantly higher potentially indicates that synthetic samples are regurgitated training samples. Comparable authenticity scores with cosine similarity implementations have been employed to gauge whether GAN-generated dermatological images are not (noisy) copies of train images." .


