###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/BayesFactors
:BayesFactors rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       :StatisticalTests ;
              rdfs:comment "Another method to test whether synthetic and real data come from similar underlying distributions is through Bayes factors. Here, we investigate whether a density estimate from a model fit on synthetic or real data is comparable. If so, the ratio between the density estimates should be close to 1. Any model can be chosen here, such as kernel density estimators or even more complex generative models like GANs and VAEs." .


