###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/CapAEs
:CapAEs rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 :AutoencoderBasedGenerationModels ;
        rdfs:comment "Capsule Autoencoders (CapAEs) leverage capsules—groups of neurons that are activated by specific features—to capture spatial hierarchies and part-whole relationships in data, enhancing both interpretability and robustness. This approach uniquely represents and processes data, making it particularly effective for tasks involving complex spatial structures. Capsules are well-suited for 3D data, capturing the complex spatial relationships inherent in three-dimensional structures, and valuable in medical imaging where 3D models of anatomical structures are common. The architecture includes dynamic routing mechanisms that facilitate the communication between capsules, ensuring that the information flow adapts dynamically based on the data. It typically employs learning rates in the range of 0.00003 to 1.0 to ensure the model converges effectively without overshooting the optimal point, authors proposed an evasion attack against CapAE by employing the RMSProp with learning rate 0.00003 and batch size 100, as well proposed a defense method by employing the Adam optimizer with learning rate 1.0 with hybrid adversarial training." .


