###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/ConAEs
:ConAEs rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 :AutoencoderBasedGenerationModels ;
        rdfs:comment "Convolutional Autoencoders (ConAEs) leverage Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) to encode and reconstruct image data, optimizing the identification of spatial hierarchies and patterns within the data. ConAEs consist of two main components: encoder and decoder; the encoder utilizes convolutional layers to capture local patterns and reduce dimensionality through pooling operations, and the decoder employs transposed convolutional layers to reconstruct the input data from the encoded representation, striving to produce output that closely resembles the original input. These are particularly effective for various computer vision tasks, including denoising, segmentation, and feature extraction. To ensure effective training and model performance, ConAEs typically employ learning rates between 0.0001 and 0.1 to stabilize training and facilitate convergence, authors used convolutional autoencoders with skip connectors by employing Adam optimizer with learning rate 0.001 and kept the batch 32 to enhance image resolution. Authors produced a deep clustering model, DEeP Embedded RegularIzed ClusTering (DEPICT), based on convolutional autoencoder and relative entropy minimization. Their model is trained on an Adam optimizer with a learning rate of 0.0001 and dropout of 0.1, which efficiently maps data into a discriminative embedding subspace and precisely predicts cluster assignments." .


