###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/DifferentialPrivacy
:DifferentialPrivacy rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              :PrivacyModels ,
                              :MetricThreshold ,
                              :Techniques ;
                     :ApplicableToTypesOfValues "All" ;
                     :DataTruthfulnessAtRecordLevel "NO" ;
                     :ReducesRiskOfInference "Partially" ;
                     :ReducesRiskOfLinking "YES" ;
                     :ReducesRiskOfSinglingout "YES" ;
                     rdfs:comment "Differential privacy (“DP”), as codified in clause 10.3, represents the most stringent privacy model by introducing mathematically calibrated noise to limit the influence of any single individual on the output. The standard details crucial considerations such as sensitivity analysis, privacy budget (ε), delta (δ), and the distinctions between local and central DP models. For project like INSAFEDARE, DP could play a strategic role in evaluating whether the synthetic-data generator exhibits memorisation or leakage, as the standard explicitly notes that DP is particularly well-suited for synthetic-data scenarios where model inversion and membership inference constitute realistic attacks." .


