###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/DiscoGAN
:DiscoGAN rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                   :GANs ;
          :GeneratesModality :ImageData ,
                             :TextData ,
                             :TimeSeriesData ;
          :UsesTechnique :CycleConsistencyLoss ,
                         :FeatureMatching ;
          rdfs:comment "Discovery GAN (DiscoGAN) facilitates the discovery of cross-domain relations by learning to translate images between domains without requiring paired samples, thus enhancing the diversity of synthetic healthcare datasets. Its methodology is thoroughly documented, detailing its architecture, cross-domain image translation mechanisms, and training procedures. It typically employs learning rates between 0.0005 and 0.05 to stabilize the training process and ensure convergence. Common batch sizes range from 32 to 128, striking a balance between computational efficiency and model performance. Various optimizers, such as Adam and RMSprop, are used to minimize loss functions. It supports various data types, including image, text, and time series data." .


