###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/DistanceToClosestRecord-DCR
:DistanceToClosestRecord-DCR rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                      :AccuracyMetrics ,
                                      :DisclosureRiskMetrics ,
                                      :RecordSimilarity ;
                             :HasModality :TabularData ,
                                          :TimeSeriesData ;
                             rdfs:comment "For disclosure risk: from target data (T) using NearestNeighbors and MIT, DCR for timeseries." ,
                                          """This metric measures how close each synthetic data point is to its nearest
neighbor within the real dataset. Here, geometric distance measures like Euclidean distance are often used. Larger distances suggest better privacy, and distances can be assessed across samples by statistics like the mean and median distance. Euclidean distance metrics have been employed in the generation of EHRs but also in generating personal/behavioral and socio-economic health data, and tabular data more generally. Gower’s distance as the non-geometric measure is also frequently employed for computing similarity for mixed-type data records, as it does not require one-hot encoding of categorical variables, for instance, in software packages like SynthEval that deal with privacy evaluation of synthetic data.""" .


