###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/DomainConstraintViolations
:DomainConstraintViolations rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                     :SanityChecks ;
                            rdfs:comment """In many instances, synthetic data should follow domain rules that are present in the real data. Examples in healthcare may be: a single patient may not receive both type 1 and type 2 diabetes diagnoses, postpartum-related diagnoses should be recorded after pregnancy diagnosis, and prostate cancer should only be recorded for biological males.


Depending on the chosen algorithm to generate synthetic data, these types of constraints might be violated. This risk is especially prevalent when using self-learning (machine learning) algorithms instead of rule-based algorithms, where constraints are more easily enforced. Checking these constraints may provide a first check on whether synthetic data is realistic""" .


