###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/EdgeCasesWithoutFailureClaim
:EdgeCasesWithoutFailureClaim rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                       :Robustness ;
                              :HasContext :ResilienceAndQuickRecoveryContext ;
                              :JustifiedBy :ModelFunctionalityGuaranteeJustification ;
                              :ProducesEvidence :LogsIndicatingMaintainedPerformanceLog ,
                                                :RobustnessTestingFrameworksLog ,
                                                :SimulatedStressEnvironmentLog ;
                              :RegulatedBy <http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#ISO/IEC25010Standard> ,
                                           :AICybersecurityChallengesStandard ;
                              rdfs:comment "Model handles edge cases without failure" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/EdgeConnect
:EdgeConnect rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                      :GANs ;
             :GeneratesModality :ImageData ;
             :UsesTechnique :AttentionSelfAttentionMechanism ;
             rdfs:comment "EdgeConnect is an advanced GAN specialized in image synthesis, particularly image inpainting. It predicts and reconstructs missing parts of images with a structured contextual understanding, generating coherent and contextually accurate visual content. The model is well-documented, detailing its architecture, training procedures, and evaluation metrics to ensure clarity and reproducibility and support various types of image data. It typically employs specific hyperparameters to optimize its performance, such as some authors employed Adam optimizer and vary the learning rates from 0.00001 to 0.0001 to train the model with a batch size 8 for image inpainting using edge prediction. Similarly, the authors employed Adam optimizer and set the initial learning rate at 0.0001 to train the model with a batch size 16 to compute the loss for GAN-based super-resolution with edge texture metric, and other authors trained the model to reshape images by setting the learning rate at 0.001 and a batch size 32." .


