###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/EstimateBias
:EstimateBias rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       :UtilityMetrics ;
              rdfs:comment "This approach measures the bias that may exist in estimating parameters from synthesized data compared to real data for a specific task. Typically, linear models are used, where a response variable of interest is regressed on a number of other variables. The overlap in estimated confidence intervals and/or divergence in coefficients is compared. More overlap and less divergence are indicators of the higher utility of the synthetic data for the specific task at issue." .


