###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/ExpertOpinion
:ExpertOpinion rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                        :SanityChecks ;
               rdfs:comment "Domain experts may be able to assess the realism of synthetic data compared to real data without making extensive statistical evaluations. Their opinion can be used as a sanity check to determine whether synthetic data is sensible within the respective domain. For example, experts can blindly score synthetic data and real data for realism on a certain scale. If similar scores are given, this can be a sign that synthetic data is sensible according to experts. However, this evaluation method has various limitations, such as high cost, vulnerability to erroneous evaluation, time-intensive, and limited scalability. Moreover, with the increase in the dimensions of the data, the evaluation becomes harder for a human." .


