###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/GPTVariants
:GPTVariants rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                      :TransformerBasedGenerativeModels ;
             :HasModality :CodeSnippetsData ,
                          :DialogueData ,
                          :TextData ;
             :UsesTechnique :BytePairEncoding ,
                            :PositionalEncoding ,
                            :SelfAttention ;
             rdfs:comment """Generative Pre-trained Transformers (GPT) and their variants, such as GPT-Neo, GPT-NeoX, and GPT-J, represent powerful large-scale transformer models pre-trained on extensive text datasets. These models excel in generating coherent and contextually relevant text for a wide array of tasks, leveraging the transformer architecture’s capabilities. GPT models are pre-trained through unsupervised learning, enabling them to capture the nuances of language and generate high-quality text. They employ a transformer architecture characterized by self-attention mechanisms and positional encodings, which allow the models to process and generate text with a deep understanding of context and sequence.
The learning rates for GPT models depend on their size and task complexity, usually fine-tuned to optimize performance. Training batch sizes vary, but larger batches are often used to stabilize training and improve convergence rates. In Ref. [280], the authors introduced GPT-NeoX, a 20-billion-parameter autoregressive language model trained on the Pile. They detailed the architecture and training of GPT-NeoX and evaluated its performance on various language-understanding, mathematics, and knowledge-based tasks. To increase training throughput, they used a batch size of approximately 3.15 million tokens, similar to OpenAI’s 175B model, and employed the ZeRO optimizer to reduce memory consumption by distributing optimizer states across ranks. GPT models utilize self-attention, positional encodings, and Byte-Pair Encoding (BPE) techniques to enhance stability [250]. Self-attention allows GPT to prioritize words within sequences, improving contextual understanding. These models are versatile and adept at processing diverse data types such as natural language text, code snippets, and dialogue systems. They excel in text generation, translation, summarization, and question-answering and are customizable for generating and completing code, benefiting software development and automated coding applications. Additionally, GPT models are utilized to create conversational agents for human-like interactions and are suitable for applications like customer service bots and virtual assistants.""" .


