###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HammingDistance
:HammingDistance rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                          :RecordSimilarity ;
                 :HasModality :TimeSeriesData ;
                 rdfs:comment "A straightforward metric of record similarity is Hamming distance, which measures the number of substitutions/edits necessary to convert one vector into another. Hamming distance has been used as a privacy metric for comparing the similarity between real and synthetic EHRs, mixed-type data such as hospital discharges and health surveys, and socio-economic health data. A threshold is often set for Hamming distance, where a distance below a given threshold indicates a stronger than desired similarity of a synthetic record with a real record." .


