                            :SimilarityMetrics ,
                            :StatisticalDistanceMeasures ;
                   :HasModality :TabularData ,
                                :TimeSeriesData ;
                   rdfs:comment """Another measure that quantifies the difference between two probability distributions is Hellinger distance. It satisfies all properties of a proper distance metric. It is
also bounded on (0,1), making it an interpretable metric. Hellinger distance is used in training and assessing generative models.""" ,
                                "For assesing similarity in tabular and timeseries data." .


