###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HybridData
:HybridData rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
            rdfs:comment """Hybrid synthetic data also combines real-world data with synthetic data [14] but differs from partially synthetic data in that only full rows or observations are real or synthetic instead of parts here. The aim is to obfuscate the identifiability of individual records while maintaining data utility. Hybrid synthetic datasets usually improve performance compared to fully and partially synthetic datasets. Each type of Data Proportion mentioned above contains unique benefits and limitations. For instance, fully synthetic data addresses data scarcity issues resulting from limited collection and ethical, legal, or privacyrelated constraints. However, since fully synthetic data often mimics statistical patterns found in real-world data, privacy risks may still exist. Partially synthetic data is useful when real-world data is abundant, but sensitive information needs to be protected. However, since observations in partially synthetic data are still directly traceable to real-world individuals, privacy risk may be higher as well. Hybrid synthetic data is able to obfuscate the identifiability of individual records while maintaining data utility. However, since hybrid synthetic data also contains entire real observations, privacy risks are often larger than for fully SD and partially
SD.""" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HybridFramework
:HybridFramework rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                          :HybridMethods ;
                 :IntegratedBy :PETs ;
                 rdfs:comment "Unlike conventional approaches that rely exclusively on statistical modelling or deep neural architectures, hybrid frameworks integrate Privacy-Enhancing Technologies (PETs) – including differential privacy and , secure computation, trusted-execution environments, and cryptographically governed training mechanisms – directly into the generative process." .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/HybridSynthetic
:HybridSynthetic rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                          :DataProportion ;
                 rdfs:comment "Hybrid synthetic data also combines real-world data with synthetic data but differs from partially synthetic data in that only full rows or observations are real or synthetic instead of parts here. The aim is to obfuscate the identifiability of individual records while maintaining data utility. Hybrid synthetic datasets usually improve performance compared to fully and partially synthetic datasets. Each type of Data Proportion mentioned above contains unique benefits and limitations. For instance, fully synthetic data addresses data scarcity issues resulting from limited collection and ethical, legal, or privacyrelated constraints. However, since fully synthetic data often mimics statistical patterns found in real-world data, privacy risks may still exist. Partially synthetic data is useful when real-world data is abundant, but sensitive information needs to be protected. However, since observations in partially synthetic data are still directly traceable to real-world individuals, privacy risk may be higher as well. Hybrid synthetic data is able to obfuscate the identifiability of individual records while maintaining data utility. However, since hybrid synthetic data also contains entire real observations, privacy risks are often larger than for fully SD and partially SD." .


