###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/JSDivergenve
:JSDivergenve rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       :StatisticalDistanceMeasures ;
              rdfs:comment """To create a symmetric and smooth divergence measure based on KL divergence, Jensen-Shannon (JS) divergence was introduced. Although JS divergence is symmetric, unlike KL divergence, it is still not a proper distance metric because it does not satisfy the triangle inequality. This inequality states that the distance between any two data points is always smaller or equal to the distance when traveling through another intermediary data point. However, when taking the square root of the JS divergence, we achieve the JS distance, which is a proper metric.
JS divergence is also widely used in training and assessing generative models.""" .


