###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/NEAEs
:NEAEs rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                :AutoencoderBasedGenerationModels ;
       rdfs:comment "Neuroevolutionary Autoencoders (NEAEs) leverage evolutionary algorithms to optimize their architectures and enhance feature extraction across complex datasets. These models use genetic algorithms for network design and training strategies, which ensures operational clarity and adaptability. The approach involves detailed documentation that covers architectural choices, training procedures, and evaluation metrics. NEAEs fine-tune their hyperparameters through adaptive evolutionary strategies, authors developed a method to search for appropriate dense blocks on image classification tasks using particle swarm optimization and train the population of autoencoders with gradient-descent-based weight updates and mutated hyperparameters, such as employed RMSProp optimizer with a batch size 256 and learning rate 0.05. They showed that RMSProp performs best instead of Adam on MNIST and Fashion-MNIST datasets. Similarly, authors produced a method that automatically initializes and adjusts hyperparameters during the training process of stacked autoencoders. They employed Adam and SGD optimizers with a learning rate of 0.005 and conducted the training layer-wise, with each new layer initiating a new neuroevolutionary optimization process. NEAEs can handle image, time series, and structured data types, making them suitable for various applications, as well as support various evolutionary techniques to optimize model performance, such as mutation and crossover functions, which enhances the model’s ability to extract and represent meaningful features from the input data." .


