###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/NNAA
:NNAA rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
               :RecordSimilarity ;
      :HasModality :TabularData ;
      rdfs:comment "The Nearest Neighbour Adversarial Accuracy (NNAA) metric gauges the trade-off between privacy and fidelity via Euclidean nearest neighbor distance. Small distances could indicate that a generator like a GAN overfits the real dataset used for training and generates synthetic data that are indistinguishable from real data. Although this means high fidelity, synthetic samples are likely close to real samples, posing privacy issues. For example, the Adversarial Accuracy metric was employed in the generation of EHRs and human genomes." .


