###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/NearestNeighborDistanceRatio-NNDR
:NearestNeighborDistanceRatio-NNDR rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                            :AccuracyMetrics ,
                                            :RecordSimilarity ;
                                   :HasModality :TimeSeriesData ;
                                   rdfs:comment "Nearest Neighbour Distance Ratio (NNDR) computes the ratio of the distance between synthetic records and the nearest real record as a ratio to the distance to the nextnearest real record. A score close to 0 indicates only a single real record is close to the synthetic record, indicating high individual record similarity. NNDR has been employed to gauge potential privacy issues due to overfitting in the generation of real-time breath data and in the generation of tabular datasets." .


