###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/PartiallySynthetic
:PartiallySynthetic rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             :DataProportion ;
                    rdfs:comment "Partially synthetic data consists of partly real-world and partly generated data within rows or observations. Here, synthetic data usually replaces sensitive and private information, whereas non-sensitive information is not replaced. For instance, Loong et al. used synthetic data to replace patients’ sensitive information in large-scale cancer survey data. Additionally, non-sensitive information may be replaced if it contains clear relationships with sensitive information and is thus a risk to data privacy protection. Common techniques to generate partially synthetic data include model-based and multiple imputation" .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/PartiallySyntheticData
:PartiallySyntheticData rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
                        rdfs:comment "Partially synthetic data consists of partly real-world and partly generated data within rows or observations. Here, synthetic data usually replaces sensitive and private information, whereas non-sensitive information is not replaced. For instance, Loong et al. used synthetic data to replace patients’ sensitive information in large-scale cancer survey data. Additionally, non-sensitive information may be replaced if it contains clear relationships with sensitive information and is thus a risk to data privacy protection. Common techniques to generate partially synthetic data include model-based and multiple imputation." .


