                 rdfs:comment "To disentangle divergence between distributions into two components, introduce a precision-recall analysis for generative models. Here, precision indicates whether the learned distribution is supported by the actual distribution, whereas recall indicates whether the learned distribution supports the actual distribution. Intuitively, precision indicates whether generated samples are likely, and recall indicates whether the diversity of generated samples resembles diversity in the original dataset. Precision-recall analyses have been used widely to assess generative models." .


