###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/ProGAN
:ProGAN rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 :GANs ;
        :GeneratesModality :ImageData ;
        :UsesTechnique :FeatureMatching ,
                       :LatentSpaceEncodingAdjustmentManipulationInterpolationRegularisation ;
        rdfs:comment "Progressive Growing GAN (ProGAN) significantly enhances image resolution progressively during training, resulting in high-fidelity synthetic images. This approach incrementally increases the resolution of the generator and discriminator, starting from a low resolution and gradually adding layers until the desired high resolution is achieved. This progressive, growing technique stabilizes the training process and leads to more detailed and realistic image synthesis. ProGAN is primarily designed to generate high-resolution images, making it particularly effective for healthcare datasets like MRI, CT scans, and X-rays. ProGAN is designed with a strong focus on transparency and reproducibility, providing comprehensive documentation detailing its architecture, training procedures, and evaluation metrics. It typically employs learning rates that can be adjusted dynamically during training to enhance stability. Authors employed the learning rate 0.03 for both generator and discriminator to train their model with batch size 32 and used Adam optimizer for inverse modeling, whereas the authors trained their model on a learning rate 0.001, bath size 64, and used Adam optimizer for prostatic cancer Gleason grade patch synthesis" .


