###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/ROE
:ROE rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
              :UtilityMetrics ;
     rdfs:comment "In this metric estimates produced with synthetic as opposed to real data, for example, proportions from frequency tables, are expressed as a ratio. The Ratio of Estimates (ROE) is a standardised score between one and zero, with one meaning that estimates from synthetic and real data align, hence indicating high utility. The ROE is only used for frequency tables and cross-tabs (and not, e.g., coefficients)." .


