                                        :NIST .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/SRGAN
:SRGAN rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                :GANs ;
       :GeneratesModality :ImageData ;
       :UsesTechnique :BatchNormalisation ;
       rdfs:comment """The Super-Resolution GAN (SRGAN) is designed to enhance the resolution of low-quality images, making it particularly valuable in fields requiring detailed image analysis, such as medical imaging. SRGAN achieves high fidelity and detailed super-resolved images through a complex architecture and meticulously tuned training protocols. SRGAN’s architecture is similar to traditional GANs but with modifications tailored for super-resolution tasks. The generator upscales low-resolution images, while the discriminator evaluates the realism of these upscaled images compared to high-resolution ground truth images. It typically employs learning rates between 0.000001 and 0.0001 to stabilize the training and ensure convergence, such as authors implemented the SRGAN for super-resolving low-resolution images by employing the batch size 16 with the learning rate of Adam is 0.0001. SRGAN can handle various image data types, such as medical and satellite imaging, to enhance the resolution of MRI, CT scans, and X-rays. It can also provide more detailed visual information for geographical and environmental analysis and improve the clarity and detail necessary for accurate diagnosis and analysis in
medical imaging.""" .


