###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/SeverityAnalysis
:SeverityAnalysis rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                           :UtilityMetrics ;
                  rdfs:comment "This is an expert-based, holistic metric of utility, where researchers evaluate themselves how ‘severely’ the performance in a particular analysis or task is affected by using synthetic data. Severity is obviously subjective and domain-dependent, but levels of severity have been expressed in the literature where, for example, ‘moderate’ severity is taken to mean a (slight) change in emphasis of an existing result instead of a different outcome. The guiding principle here is that using synthetic data should not lead to markedly different inferences from the data by stakeholders." .


