###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/StyleGAN
:StyleGAN rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                   :GANs ;
          :GeneratesModality :ImageData ;
          :UsesTechnique :FeatureMatching ,
                         :LatentSpaceEncodingAdjustmentManipulationInterpolationRegularisation ;
          rdfs:comment """StyleGAN is a renowned generative model for its ability to produce photorealistic, high-resolution images, especially of complex subjects like facial features. By leveraging a unique layered architecture, StyleGAN allows for precise control over various aspects of image synthesis, enabling the generation of diverse and detailed
outputs. The model’s design and training procedures are meticulously documented, ensuring transparency and reproducibility in its application. It employs several hyperparameters and training techniques to achieve its high-quality outputs, such as typically setting the learning rate around 0.001 to maintain the balance between convergence speed and stability during training. It commonly uses Adam optimizer to stabilize the training process and 8 to 256 Batch Size to manage the memory consumption while maintaining the quality of generated images. Authors employed StyleGAN to manipulate the latent space, using Adam optimizer with a batch size decrease from 256 to 8 on a learning rate of 0.001 for the synthesis of high-resolution medical images. In some cases, the batch size increased to 2048 for large-scale data, authors employed a batch size of 2048 and trained the model on a learning rate of 0.002 for large-scale text-to-image synthesis. StyleGAN’s versatility makes it suitable for various image data types, such as generating high-resolution and photorealistic images, making it ideal for fashion, entertainment, and virtual reality applications. It can also be adapted for generating synthetic medical images such as MRI or CT scans, assisting in data augmentation and training of medical diagnostic systems.""" .


