###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/SynthVAE
:SynthVAE rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                   :AutoencoderBasedGenerationModels ;
          rdfs:comment """SynthVAE is a variational autoencoder developed to generate high-quality synthetic tabular data, focusing on privacy and fairness to facilitate machine learning applications within the National Health Service (NHS), United Kingdom. It addresses the challenges of sensitive healthcare data by using techniques like Gaussian Mixture Model pre-processing for non-Gaussian variables and hyperparameter tuning. The model aims to balance data fidelity and privacy, making it a viable alternative to GANs, with the added benefits of interpretability
and user control. Authors developed VAE for generating high-fidelity, privacy-preserving, and fair synthetic tabular data for healthcare applications. Based on previous work, the author incorporated Gaussian Mixture
Models (GMM) for transforming non-Gaussian continuous variables into Gaussian distributions, leveraging the GMMTransformer from the Reversible Data Transforms (RDT) library. The Optuna library was used for hyperparameter tuning and early stopping. An example use case using a heart failure prediction dataset involves training a decision tree classifier to assess data quality and fairness. Key model configurations include latent dimensions of 108 (SUPPORT) and 104 (Medical Information Mart for Intensive Care (MIMIC-III)) and hidden dimensions of 640 (SUPPORT) and 896 (MIMIC-III). Furthermore, authors addressed the challenge of generating synthetic healthcare data that preserves privacy and utility. Using VAE, they developed a model to create realistic synthetic data while incorporating differential privacy and fairness assessments. The methodology includes regularizing the autoencoder to avoid overfitting, encoding raw data as distributions, and hyper tuning the model for different data types. Their experimental work involved assessing the model’s performance, exploring privacy-enhancing technologies, such as homomorphic encryption and federated learning, and planning production-level tool development within NHS. SynthVAE is tailored to generate synthetic tabular data, specifically handling continuous and categorical variables. It focuses on accurately replicating the structure and relationships in single-table healthcare datasets. It utilizes VAEs with differential privacy to generate synthetic tabular data, as well as incorporates GMM pre-processing for handling non-Gaussian variables and employs hyperparameter tuning and early stopping to optimize model performance.""" .


