###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/TCloseness
:TCloseness rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                     :MetricThreshold ;
            :HasModality :TabularData ;
            :HasRoleCompliance :ProtectionAgainstSkewnessAttacks ;
            :RegulatedBy <http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD#ISO/IEC20889Standard> ;
            :HasMetricValue """For Grouped-Based Privacy Models

t<=0.2 - Acceptable distributional fistance
t <=0.1 - Strong protection""" ;
            rdfs:comment "Measures distributional distance of sensitive attributes." ,
                         "T-closeness further refines the model by imposing a constraint on the distance between the distribution of sensitive attributes within an equivalence class and the global distribution. ISO/IEC 20889 emphasises this requirement for contexts – such as oncology, rare-disease cohorts, or demographic minorities – where sensitive attributes may have uneven population distributions, thereby enabling attackers to exploit distributional deviations." .


