###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/TLSCertificatesLog
:TLSCertificatesLog rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             :DataTransitEvidence .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/TRTS
:TRTS rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
               :EfficiencyMetrics ,
               :SimilarityMetrics ,
               :UtilityMetrics ;
      :HasModality :TabularData ,
                   :TimeSeriesData ;
      rdfs:comment "For efficiency - tabular data." ,
                   "In contrast to the TSTR approach, the Train Real Test Synthetic (TRTS) approach evaluates a model trained on real data on a synthetic test set. The goal is to assess whether an algorithm trained on real data achieves good performance on synthetic data. This metric indicates whether the synthetic data generating model has succeeded in generating realistic labels, and can thus also be seen as a fidelity metric. However, there are also instances where this can be a task-specific utility metric; namely, when synthetic data is used as test data for a pretrained algorithm. For this reason, we classify TRTS as a utility rather than fidelity metric, although it can also be regarded as the latter." .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/TSRTR
:TSRTR rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                :UtilityMetrics ;
       :HasModality :TimeSeriesData ;
       rdfs:comment "Downstream Task. By training aReinforcement Learning (RL) model, analyzing privacy-utility trade-off, first-order temporal statistics, diagnosis forecastanalysis, latent temporal statistics, and by training on real test on real and training on synthetic test on real data, andcomparing the 2 performances with cosine similarity between the MAEs obtained." .


###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/TSTR
:TSTR rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
               :EfficiencyMetrics ,
               :SimilarityMetrics ,
               :UtilityMetrics ;
      :HasModality :TabularData ,
                   :TimeSeriesData ;
      rdfs:comment "For assesing similarity in tabular and timeseries data." ,
                   "For efficiency - tabular data." ,
                   "To assess whether synthetic data can be used instead of real data in a practical setting, introduced the Train Synthetic Test Real (TSTR) methodology. Here, they train an algorithm on synthetic data and assess its generalization capabilities on a real test set. The performance is compared with an algorithm trained on real data. If performance is comparable, synthetic data is useful for training algorithms instead of real data when real data cannot be used." .


