###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/TotalVariationDistance
:TotalVariationDistance rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                 :StatisticalDistanceMeasures ;
                        rdfs:comment "Equating to the largest absolute difference between two probability distributions, the Total Variation Distance is another proper distance metric. It is related to the Hellinger distance, as the squared Hellinger distance provides a lower bound, and the Hellinger distance multiplied by √2 provides an upper bound of the Total Variation Distance. Total Variation Distance has been used to assess the quality of generative models" .


