###  http://www.semanticweb.org/ek279783/ontologies/2025/8/ontologySD/VanillaGAN
:VanillaGAN rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                     :GANs ;
            :GeneratesModality :ImageData ,
                               :TextData ,
                               :TimeSeriesData ;
            :UsesTechnique :BatchNormalisation ,
                           :LabelSmoothing ;
            rdfs:comment "Vanilla GANs employ a traditional architecture consisting of a generator and a discriminator to produce images that closely resemble authentic ones, fostering straightforward image synthesis. The simplicity of Vanilla GANs makes them a valuable starting point for generative modeling, offering a clear framework for understanding the principles of adversarial training. It maintains transparency with well-documented methodologies, standard training procedures, and evaluation metrics. Authors used mean field theory to train a 200-layer vanilla GAN on MNIST and Fashion-MNIST datasets by setting the hyperparameters, such as the optimization method is Adam, learning rate is 0.00001, and bath size is 128, and validated that their model can produce high-quality images. Vanilla GAN supports various data types, including image, text, and time series data." .


